      "description": "**Role:** Handles ProductUpdated; evicts that product's entry from the cache.\n**Risk:** concurrency-sensitive, cache correctness\n\n**Look for:** eviction happens inside the same handler that processes the update event, with no ordering guarantee relative to the DB transaction that produced it.\n\n**Discussion:** is eviction guaranteed to happen after the update transaction commits, or could a reader hit the cache and get the old value in between? (🔴 Blocking)"
    }
